msm: flush dirtyfb for CPU-written framebuffers on continuously-scanned displays.

msm_framebuffer_dirtyfb() skipped the flush whenever no attached plane had asked
for one (refcount_read(&dirtyfb) == 1), on the reasoning that a display which
scans out continuously picks up pixel changes by itself.  That is true for GPU
writes, which are coherent through the IOMMU, but not for buffers that someone
has mapped for CPU access: those writes only become visible to the display when
a commit publishes them.

Measured on liuqin (Xiaomi Pad 6 Pro, SM8475; two video-mode DSI panels, driver
mode_flags MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO, dpu encoder intf mode INTF_MODE_VIDEO).  The
fbdev console draws through the deferred ops and reaches this function with
refcount_read(&dirtyfb) == 1, so drm_atomic_helper_dirtyfb() was never called:
per-draw flushing never happened and the panel kept showing stale content until
some unrelated commit, even though the damage chain (sys_* -> damage ->
damage_work -> fb_dirty) ran fine.  Instrumented counts on the unit were
damage=80, work=80, fb_dirty=160, msm_fb_dirty=204 and msm_dirtyfb=160, all
160 skipping.

With the skip extended to require that nothing has the buffer CPU-mapped,
console lines appear on the panel as they are drawn.

Not upstream: 7.2.5 and the community liuqin tree carry the unconditional skip.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fb.c
@@ -39,11 +39,21 @@
 				   unsigned int num_clips)
 {
 	struct msm_framebuffer *msm_fb = to_msm_framebuffer(fb);
+	struct msm_gem_object *msm_obj = to_msm_bo(fb->obj[0]);
 
 	/* If this fb is not used on any display requiring pixel data to be
-	 * flushed, then skip dirtyfb
+	 * flushed, then skip dirtyfb.  That reasoning only holds for buffers
+	 * the display engine already sees, i.e. ones written through the
+	 * GPU: a display that scans out continuously picks GPU writes up by
+	 * itself.  It does not hold for buffers someone has mapped for CPU
+	 * access, because those writes are only published to the display by a
+	 * commit.  Measured on liuqin (SM8475, two video-mode DSI panels):
+	 * the fbdev console draws through the deferred ops and arrives here
+	 * with refcount_read(&dirtyfb) == 1, and with the unconditional skip
+	 * the panel keeps showing stale content until an unrelated commit,
+	 * while committing here makes every batch of drawn lines appear.
 	 */
-	if (refcount_read(&msm_fb->dirtyfb) == 1)
+	if (refcount_read(&msm_fb->dirtyfb) == 1 && !msm_obj->vmap_count)
 		return 0;
 
 	return drm_atomic_helper_dirtyfb(fb, file_priv, flags, color,
